   "hypothesis_id": "H3",
   "mechanism": "INPP5D acts as a protective repressor in microglia by inhibiting the expression of RIPK1 kinase. By repressing RIPK1, INPP5D limits the production of diverse proinflammatory mediators that would otherwise drive neuroinflammation. Protective variants in INPP5D (such as rs10933431-G) may enhance this repression, thereby mitigating late-onset Alzheimer's disease risk factors and slowing disease progression.",
